code: 0
--- stdout
Process from .github/dojo.toml: board acme/3, issues in acme/shop.
Find an issue to take with gh dojo next (Todo or no status, no unresolved blockers);
read it with gh dojo show <N>.
Run a verb as gh dojo <verb> <N>; --dry-run shows its plan first.
Every command takes --json (schema_version 1), --jq and --template, as gh does.

Verbs:
  start       You begin working on the issue
              sprint: today's iteration
  done        выкачено на прод
              also on closed issues; sprint: the iteration of the day it entered Ready
  plan        Take the issue into the current sprint
              sprint: today's iteration
  unplan      Take the issue out of its sprint
              clears the sprint; an issue not on the board stays off it
  triage      The issue is triaged
              sets Estimate 3, Priority P1

Every verb adds the issue to the board if it is missing and refuses a
closed issue unless noted. A repeat is safe: an effect already in place
(status, sprint, fields, comment, labels, assignee, blocked-by link,
closed or open) is skipped.

Lifecycle (from → to):
  start       any status → In progress
  done        any status → Done
  plan        any status → status unchanged
  unplan      any status → status unchanged
  triage      any status → status unchanged
  Initial:    Todo (new issues; also an issue with no status or not on the board)
  Final:      Done (gh dojo list hides it unless --all)

Exit codes:
  0  everything applied: go on
  1  bad arguments or config: fix them as the error says
  2  a process check refused: don't work around it; ask the user
  3  issue or board not found: check the number (gh dojo list) or board.owner/project in .github/dojo.toml
  4  network, rate limit or auth: retry later, or gh auth refresh -s project
  5  partially applied: re-run the same command; it finishes the rest
--- stderr
